1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,361
The external pressure came as a detailed report from the city.

2
00:00:03,361 --> 00:00:11,836
One member of the committee, a very attentive woman, wrote that the project had been neglectful of its own staff.

3
00:00:11,836 --> 00:00:16,016
“You cannot continue like this,” she said.

4
00:00:16,016 --> 00:00:21,796
“The number of unpaid hours is a scandal, not a virtue.”

5
00:00:21,796 --> 00:00:25,052
The accusation was partly fair.

6
00:00:25,052 --> 00:00:35,217
Behind the small office, an elderly diner kept a ledger of every hour they had worked, and the total was a challenge to their own honesty.

7
00:00:35,217 --> 00:00:39,832
“We are in a siege of our own making,” Maya said.

8
00:00:39,832 --> 00:00:46,017
“Since the report has been filed, all we can do is answer it.”

9
00:00:46,017 --> 00:00:59,223
A champion of the project, a communicative woman with a possessive streak, proposed a fight: raise the fee, commit the council, and let the quarrel become public.

10
00:00:59,223 --> 00:01:03,098
“That is a provocative move,” Lin said.

11
00:01:03,098 --> 00:01:05,968
“It is also a slippery one.

12
00:01:05,968 --> 00:01:11,138
Haste would dampen the very thing we are trying to prove.”

13
00:01:11,138 --> 00:01:15,149
The moderate path was harder than the visionary one.

14
00:01:15,149 --> 00:01:28,429
It meant a cubic metre of space instead of an office, a part-time electrician instead of a team, an electric kettle instead of a kitchen, and a moderate fee for the volunteers.

15
00:01:28,429 --> 00:01:37,789
“We must not neglect the needy member of this group,” she said, “and we must not rub salt into the wound either.”

16
00:01:37,789 --> 00:01:43,644
The sitting ended with a compromise and a maiden speech from the youngest volunteer.

17
00:01:43,644 --> 00:02:08,465
“Diligence is not the same as obedience,” she said, “and a feverish week is not a plan.” The ball was in the council's court; she really did threaten to resign, and the affectionate letter that followed did not change the dimensional cast of the problem: a contest between a prison of small habits and a situated, human schedule.

18
00:02:08,465 --> 00:02:18,725
The squeeze was on the budget, not on her patience, and the question was whether the electric bill counted as a part of the project's true dimension.

19
00:02:18,725 --> 00:02:29,340
She wrote that sentence twice, and then a third time, because a dimension she could not name was exactly the thing that had defeated them in March.

20
00:02:29,340 --> 00:02:35,560
They had committed themselves to a smaller scope and a clearer scenery of responsibility.

21
00:02:35,560 --> 00:02:44,691
“Than the last one,” Lin added, “which is to say: better, when you can tell the difference.”
